{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"playwright-scraper","displayName":"Playwright Scraper","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/3coco3/skills/playwright-scraper","publisherHandle":"3coco3","publisherDisplayName":"xiaofu","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/3coco3","version":"1.0.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1772761294752,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/playwright-scraper/card?ownerHandle=3coco3&version=1.0.0","sha256":"3776094d375fcc6efe8b70d3910810546b04459b8774496a5bd94a1bab59840a","size":1890,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"65f88ae5ffae15467b3c7310610762d2ee2402602ed3de94765f0bdefee5afe1","bundleFingerprints":["f4bc476e80a4cde5d90751fff65cbe2614cbc561c9db80974a5bce1e8b805428","b5d6432744a3af91f2b781a28431cbd5bc4dfd1e1d6a76d5e41701d6dd73c9fc"],"files":[{"path":"index.js","size":1479,"sha256":"7ff49f430f0d3669e7a8400d5f91410bcc8a166b2b9a57c50c715d7c186b62f8","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"package-lock.json","size":57188,"sha256":"5583e7cfb558d85cb47353fb8c33e1e5834864f16fa3742826089fbc3bf7a37a","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"package.json","size":205,"sha256":"37e8634a6fac36c6d511e39aa1f6d057fb1c753add1701b63f8a816234f730e1","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":625,"sha256":"55fdd05373b5679a6c7a304733cf83fc4af32ff01db1f41c9368b09691e18986","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":208,"sha256":"5a38f0d49de97019966764add5b517878561a225515e2f3eeab3b7b07eadf69c","contentType":"application/json"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is an unrestricted anti-bot web scraper, and its URL input can be abused to run local shell commands.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789106972130,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"OS Command Injection Through the URL Argument"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"index.js"},"region":{"startLine":26,"endLine":29}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"8d7f31099fde3b55"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `index.js`, lines 26–29  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: OS command injection  \n  **Risk Level**: Critical\n\n  ### Vulnerable Code\n\n  ```js\n  const url = request.params.arguments.url;\n  try {\n    // Execute the scraper script and capture its output\n    const stdout = execSync(`node scripts/playwright-stealth.js \"${url}\"`, { encoding: 'utf8' });\n  ```\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The `stealth_scrape` MCP tool accepts an attacker-controlled `url` value and interpolates it directly into a command string passed to `child_process.execSync()`. This API executes the string through a system shell.\n\n  Wrapping the value in double quotes does not make it safe. An attacker can include a double quote to terminate the intended argument and then append shell operators and arbitrary commands. Neither the MCP input schema nor the request handler validates the value as an HTTP/HTTPS URL or safely escapes it for the host shell.\n\n  The referenced `scripts/playwright-stealth.js` file is absent from the audited package. Although this prevents the advertised scraper from operating normally, it does not reliably mitigate the injection: the shell can still parse and execute appended commands.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. An attacker or compromised agent invokes the exposed `stealth_scrape` MCP tool.\n  2. The attacker supplies a crafted `url`, for example:\n     ```text\n     \"; id; #\n     ```\n  3. The server constructs a command equivalent to:\n     ```sh\n     node scripts/playwright-stealth.js \"\"; id; #\"\n     ```\n  4. `execSync()` passes that command to the system shell.\n  5. The shell executes the injected `id` command under the MCP server process's operating-system identity.\n  6. An attacker can replace `id` with other commands available to that account.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  Successful exploitation provides arbitrary command execution with the privileges of the Node.js MCP server. The attacker could read or alter files accessible to that account, access environment variables and locally stored credentials, execute installed programs, make network connections, or modify project and user data.\n\n  The exact scope depends on how the server is deployed. If it runs under a privileged account or has access to sensitive host resources, the resulting compromise may extend to those resources. No independent privilege-escalation mechanism was identified in the audited files.","severity":"Critical"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Do not construct a shell command using user-controlled data. Invoke Node.js directly with an argument array and disable shell processing:\n     ```js\n     import { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\n\n     const stdout = execFileSync(\n       process.execPath,\n       [\"scripts/playwright-stealth.js\", validatedUrl],\n       {\n         encoding: \"utf8\",\n         shell: false,\n         timeout: 30_000,\n         maxBuffer: 5 * 1024 * 1024\n       }\n     );\n     ```\n\n  2. Parse and validate the input before execution:\n     ```js\n     function validateUrl(value) {\n       if (typeof value !== \"string\" || value.length > 2048) {\n         throw new Error(\"Invalid URL\");\n       }\n\n       const parsed = new URL(value);\n       if (![\"http:\", \"https:\"].includes(parsed.protocol)) {\n         throw new Error(\"Only HTTP and HTTPS URLs are allowed\");\n       }\n\n       return parsed.href;\n     }\n     ```\n\n  3. Consider blocking loopback, link-local, private-network, and cloud metadata destinations if arbitrary internal-resource access is not an intended feature.\n\n  4. Run the browser and MCP process under a dedicated, unprivileged account with filesystem and network restrictions.\n\n  5. Add regression tests using quote characters, command separators, command substitutions, newlines, and platform-specific shell metacharacters.\n\n  6. Include and review the referenced scraper script before deployment; the audited package does not contain `scripts/playwright-stealth.js`."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":0,"primaryLanguage":"JSON","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789106887.2803814,"endTime":1789106939.0900657}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"unknown","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v5757m52j3x5hztmyz7xqhvvq58e7w36-ealyXJ/clawscan-skillspector-153378655/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T06:08:06.528902+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":80,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":16,"executable":false,"size_bytes":625,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"_meta.json","type":"json","lines":8,"executable":false,"size_bytes":208,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"index.js","type":"javascript","lines":38,"executable":true,"size_bytes":1479,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"package-lock.json","type":"json","lines":1606,"executable":false,"size_bytes":57188,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"package.json","type":"json","lines":9,"executable":false,"size_bytes":205,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-f93fd91cb5c64ddab9680bf1f8d14b2e","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: brace-expansion==1.1.12 — 4 advisory(ies): CVE-2026-13149 (brace-expansion: DoS via exponential-time expansion of consecutive non-expanding); CVE-2026-33750 (brace-expansion: Zero-step sequence causes process hang and memory exhaustion); CVE-2026-14257 (brace-expansion: DoS via unbounded expansion length causing an out-of-memory pro) +1 more","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":167,"end_line":null},"finding":"brace-expansion==1.1.12","explanation":"brace-expansion 1.1.12 is a known vulnerable version with multiple denial-of-service advisories involving pathological expansion inputs. Because it is present in the lockfile, any runtime path that accepts attacker-controlled glob or brace patterns could trigger excessive CPU or memory consumption.","remediation":"Upgrade brace-expansion to a patched version, typically by updating dependent packages such as minimatch/glob/rimraf to current supported releases. Avoid feeding user-controlled patterns into globbing or brace expansion logic, and add input length/complexity limits.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"b33c7f91e76a07e38abe7d11ad00f2b25f6104d51dd19a46a16d32143fd46a30","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":167,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-5eaf73c457ef4fe69a14c13a5c2afc86","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: express-rate-limit==8.2.1 — 1 advisory(ies): CVE-2026-30827 (express-rate-limit: IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses bypass per-client rate limiting o)","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":481,"end_line":null},"finding":"express-rate-limit==8.2.1","explanation":"express-rate-limit 8.2.1 is affected by an advisory allowing rate-limit bypass using IPv4-mapped IPv6 address forms. In a scraper skill that may expose an MCP/HTTP interface through the SDK stack, bypassable rate limiting can materially weaken abuse protection and permit brute force or request flooding from a single client.","remediation":"Upgrade express-rate-limit to a fixed version and normalize client IP addresses before rate-limit keying. Validate proxy trust settings carefully and add secondary abuse controls such as authentication, global quotas, and upstream WAF or reverse-proxy throttling.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c888219b6bc32f73e1f71c0539b462faee9f7c635599b16bcf04a31d28ff755b","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":481,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-44b89f23dedc46c98a87af6a33d92806","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: fast-uri==3.1.0 — 7 advisory(ies): CVE-2026-13676 (fast-uri vulnerable to host confusion via failed IDN canonicalization); CVE-2026-18446 (fast-uri vulnerable to host confusion via backslash authority introducer); CVE-2026-75975 (fast-uri vulnerable to server-side request forgery via malformed IPv6 normalizat) +4 more","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":505,"end_line":null},"finding":"fast-uri==3.1.0","explanation":"fast-uri 3.1.0 is a known-affected version with multiple host confusion and SSRF-related advisories. In the context of a browser automation/scraper skill, URI parsing errors are more dangerous because the skill is likely to process remote URLs, and malformed input could influence outbound requests, target validation, or allowlist checks.","remediation":"Upgrade fast-uri to a patched release through direct or transitive dependency updates. Review all URL validation, canonicalization, and allowlist logic to use a hardened parser consistently, and reject malformed or ambiguous host representations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"30f9c4426e4e581297beaf6d0f65339713b650106cdad4a39f10f1a25b26adee","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":505,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-a4c3ae17c5564641b91de3e8399bc0f4","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: hono==4.12.5 — 16 advisory(ies): CVE-2026-56762 (Hono missing validation of cookie name on write path in setCookie()); CVE-2026-47676 (Hono: app.mount() strips mount prefix using undecoded path, causing incorrect ro); CVE-2026-47675 (Hono: Cookie helper does not sanitize sameSite and priority, allowing Set-Cookie) +13 more","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":710,"end_line":null},"finding":"hono==4.12.5","explanation":"hono 4.12.5 has numerous listed advisories affecting cookies, routing, and request handling behavior. Because @modelcontextprotocol/sdk depends on Hono and may expose server functionality, flaws in request parsing or route handling could become reachable from remote clients and have meaningful security consequences.","remediation":"Upgrade hono to a patched version by updating the SDK or overriding the vulnerable transitive dependency where safe. Re-test route matching, cookie handling, mount behavior, and any middleware relying on normalized paths after upgrading.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e11bd050f82ca562f1cd946285de663adc75d75182bb9529134d695153c41020","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":710,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-f2c46af5cf8f493d8c652460a8738a7a","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: ip-address==10.0.1 — 2 advisory(ies): CVE-2026-69192 (ip-address: Address4 decodes leading-zero octets as decimal while resolvers deco); CVE-2026-42338 (ip-address has XSS in Address6 HTML-emitting methods)","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":772,"end_line":null},"finding":"ip-address==10.0.1","explanation":"ip-address 10.0.1 is flagged for address parsing inconsistencies and XSS in HTML-emitting methods. In this dependency tree it is used by express-rate-limit, and parsing inconsistencies can directly affect IP-based security decisions, making bypass of per-client controls plausible in server-exposed skill deployments.","remediation":"Upgrade ip-address to a fixed version, preferably by updating express-rate-limit or applying a safe override. Avoid using library-generated HTML output, normalize IP representations before comparison, and add regression tests for leading-zero and IPv4-mapped IPv6 cases.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"271a0dc302dc33465b9262aa4ceb0507549ad5f8292ab8a1b2d3838c999b169b","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":772,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-2ed90768f7284e8f943a054c66d94517","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: path-to-regexp==8.3.0 — 2 advisory(ies): CVE-2026-4923 (path-to-regexp vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service via multiple w); CVE-2026-4926 (path-to-regexp vulnerable to Denial of Service via sequential optional groups)","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":1079,"end_line":null},"finding":"path-to-regexp==8.3.0","explanation":"path-to-regexp 8.3.0 has reported ReDoS/DoS issues involving complex route patterns. Since it underpins router behavior in the server stack, attacker-crafted paths may trigger excessive processing and degrade availability if the skill exposes HTTP endpoints.","remediation":"Upgrade path-to-regexp via router/express dependency updates to a patched release. Audit route patterns for excessive optional groups or wildcard complexity, and enforce request timeouts and upstream rate limiting to reduce DoS exposure.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"58e9d75e6b0380e8106d00aa94273dadbd3c17b21126e3fd583e3e39d308b23a","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":1079,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-5c24fcdbfe8849a6969ffce9b9a9db30","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":12},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill explicitly advertises anti-bot evasion, stealth behavior, user-agent spoofing, and scraping arbitrary URLs, but provides no warning about legal, ethical, or security risks. This makes misuse more likely by normalizing bypass of website protections and enabling users to target any site without guardrails or disclosure of the consequences.","remediation":"Add clear user-facing warnings that the tool performs bot-detection evasion and must only be used on sites the user is authorized to access and scrape. Restrict or document allowed use cases, require explicit acknowledgement for arbitrary-URL scraping, and describe compliance requirements such as respecting site terms, robots policies where applicable, rate limits, and applicable law.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":12}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-e9d34edadaee44e381a63dd46b36bef2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"_meta.json","start_line":7,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest description is written only in Chinese, which imposes a specific language choice in the skill's natural-language metadata. There is no indication of user opt-in, multilingual support, or a documented region-specific justification for this locale constraint.","remediation":"Provide the description in the default expected language for the environment, add multilingual metadata, or explicitly document that the skill is intended only for a Chinese-language/region-specific context.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"_meta.json","start_line":7,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-f70bbbe994434dfe9713a0d03142aff9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"index.js","start_line":12,"end_line":16},"finding":null,"explanation":"The natural-language strings describing the tool and its input are written only in Chinese, which effectively imposes a locale/language choice without offering alternatives or opt-in. The file does not document a region-specific purpose that would justify this restriction under the stated policy.","remediation":"Provide bilingual or locale-neutral descriptions, or explicitly document that the skill is intended for Chinese-speaking users with a justified scope. If applicable, offer language selection or note the supported language in a user-visible way.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"index.js","start_line":12,"end_line":16}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-30c0b021194d438e8b3a2cc1d62d5084","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"index.js","start_line":29,"end_line":29},"finding":null,"explanation":"The tool passes a user-controlled URL directly into a shell command via execSync string interpolation. Even though the URL is wrapped in double quotes, shell metacharacter expansion and quoting edge cases can still enable command injection or unintended command execution, especially in a stdio-exposed MCP tool where input may be attacker-controlled.","remediation":"Do not build shell commands with interpolated user input. Replace execSync with execFileSync or spawnSync using an argument array, validate the URL with a strict allowlist of protocols/format, and consider invoking the Playwright script directly as a module instead of via a shell. Add explicit user/admin approval and logging for outbound browsing actions if this tool is exposed to untrusted prompts.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"index.js","start_line":29,"end_line":29}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-f9ee8a71aed64b22ae734a742f498a8e","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: @hono/node-server==1.19.11 — 2 advisory(ies): CVE-2026-39406 (@hono/node-server: Middleware bypass via repeated slashes in serveStatic); GHSA-frvp-7c67-39w9 (Node.js Adapter for Hono: Path traversal in `serve-static` on Windows via encode)","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":15,"end_line":null},"finding":"@hono/node-server==1.19.11","explanation":"The lockfile includes @hono/node-server 1.19.11, and the cited advisories affect static file serving behavior such as repeated-slash middleware bypass and Windows path traversal in serve-static handling. Even though this file alone does not prove the vulnerable code path is used, a dependency lockfile pinning a known-affected version is a real supply-chain risk because the package may be invoked by the skill at runtime.","remediation":"Upgrade @hono/node-server to a version that fixes the referenced advisories, and regenerate the lockfile. If static file serving is not needed, remove or disable serveStatic-related functionality and review any Windows path handling and URL normalization logic.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7eaa6a55b7843ff1512af1aa6a672e7951edc5aa751583158b5643a53aeb197b","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":15,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-e9bbc22c3b564974a5fcfbd8786186cf","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: body-parser==2.2.2 — 1 advisory(ies): CVE-2026-12590 (body-parser vulnerable to denial of service when invalid limit value silently di)","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.82,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":143,"end_line":null},"finding":"body-parser==2.2.2","explanation":"body-parser 2.2.2 is listed in the dependency tree and has a reported denial-of-service issue around invalid limit handling. This is a true vulnerable dependency finding, although its practical impact depends on whether untrusted request bodies are parsed by an exposed HTTP endpoint in the skill.","remediation":"Upgrade body-parser to a patched release via updating the parent dependency chain and refreshing package-lock.json. Also enforce strict request size limits and reject malformed parser configuration values in the application.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ae27e150558a2356a99c966d7d2bf4685e93afff0b6fcac8a889fc85fdaa2c88","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":143,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-1eaf363501524d7bad70d07ff090dbc6","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: qs==6.15.0 — 3 advisory(ies): CVE-2026-82417 (qs: Denial of Service via Attacker Controlled isBuffer); CVE-2026-8723 (qs has a remotely triggerable DoS: qs.stringify crashes with TypeError on null/u); CVE-2026-82562 (qs array-limit bypass via bracket-key comma parsing)","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":1241,"end_line":null},"finding":"qs==6.15.0","explanation":"qs 6.15.0 is present and has advisories related to denial of service and parser edge cases. This is a true vulnerable dependency, but impact is lower unless the skill accepts attacker-controlled query strings or nested parameter structures through an exposed web interface.","remediation":"Upgrade qs to a patched version through express/body-parser updates or dependency overrides. Constrain query parser depth, parameter count, and input size, and disable rich query parsing if not required.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c61eec4265be230fb6f8502303ece451d0c7810443170c474368c47bd501c2d1","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":1241,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-ed9f012bf8434860b4a7ae520cd75652","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":5,"end_line":null},"finding":"\"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"^1.27.1\"","explanation":"The dependency uses a caret range, which permits automatic installation of newer compatible releases rather than a single exact version. This increases supply-chain risk because a compromised or breaking upstream release could be pulled into builds without explicit review, though the package.json alone does not show active exploitation.","remediation":"Pin the dependency to an exact version in package.json and use a lockfile committed to source control. For stronger assurance, enable dependency auditing, review updates before adoption, and consider integrity verification or an internal registry mirror.","code_snippet":"  \"name\": \"playwright-scraper\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"^1.27.1\",\n    \"playwright-extra\": \"^4.3.6\",\n    \"puppeteer-extra-plugin-stealth\": \"^2.11.2\"\n  }","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"baf6637ab1ea943517219be50cf13c0478b24506a049ee541614d120aa58a389","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":5,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-786e6a81471441e79370bde4a1b73ff3","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":6,"end_line":null},"finding":"\"playwright-extra\": \"^4.3.6\"","explanation":"The dependency is not pinned to an exact version, so future installs may resolve to different upstream releases. In this skill context, that is somewhat more dangerous because browser automation and scraping tooling are high-value targets for supply-chain compromise and often execute powerful local code during runtime.","remediation":"Replace the caret version with an exact version and commit a lockfile to ensure deterministic installs. Also restrict updates to reviewed release bumps, run npm audit or equivalent scanning in CI, and consider vendor approval policies for automation-related packages.","code_snippet":"  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"^1.27.1\",\n    \"playwright-extra\": \"^4.3.6\",\n    \"puppeteer-extra-plugin-stealth\": \"^2.11.2\"\n  }\n}","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"dd2a14fc1ff164f7494f64e9da2c4a10bd15efd1d05a897c7e0455a232b0533f","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":6,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-97412be634c048d9a32e84eb23ec3e2f","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":7,"end_line":null},"finding":"\"puppeteer-extra-plugin-stealth\": \"^2.11.2\"","explanation":"The stealth plugin is specified with a caret range, allowing newer upstream versions to be installed automatically. This is more sensitive in context because a stealth/evasion-focused browser plugin has elevated abuse potential and, if compromised, could alter scraping behavior, exfiltrate data, or execute malicious code in environments running the skill.","remediation":"Pin the package to an exact version and commit the package lockfile so installations remain reproducible. Additionally, review this dependency carefully, minimize use of stealth/evasion packages unless necessary, and gate all dependency updates through manual review and automated supply-chain scanning.","code_snippet":"  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"^1.27.1\",\n    \"playwright-extra\": \"^4.3.6\",\n    \"puppeteer-extra-plugin-stealth\": \"^2.11.2\"\n  }\n}","intent":null,"ta